course: dictionary
lesson: 12957
title: Excrement: the formal word for poo
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: «Excrement» is the formal word for poo: the solid waste that leaves the body of a person or an animal. Scientists use it in lessons about digestion, which is how the body breaks down food and gets rid of what it cannot use.
explain: «The scientists collected the excrement to find out what the wild deer had been eating.» The clues are scientists, collected and find out. This is a careful, serious word, so it fits a science report or a book about animals.
explain: In everyday talk, people say poo, droppings or mess. You will hear «excrement» mostly in science lessons or in books about nature, not at the dinner table.
explain: Safety comes first. Never touch excrement with bare hands. «Always wash your hands after cleaning the cat's litter tray.»
fact: Excrement means solid waste that comes out of the body of a person or an animal.
fact: Excrement is a formal word; poo, droppings and mess mean much the same in everyday talk.
fact: Scientists study animal excrement, also called droppings or scat, to learn what animals eat.
fact: Never touch excrement with your bare hands, and wash your hands after cleaning a pet's litter.
fact: Excrement is uncountable, so you say «some excrement», not «an excrement».
exercise: «The scientists studied the excrement to learn what the fox had eaten.» What does excrement mean? | A soft, furry coat | Food that an animal has not yet eaten | The noise an animal makes | *Solid waste that comes out of an animal's body
exercise: Which everyday word means about the same as excrement? | *Poo | Whisper | Breakfast | Lunch
exercise: Why do scientists study animal excrement? | To make it into a new paint colour | To use it as a game piece | *To learn what animals eat | To hide it from other people
test: What should you do after cleaning a pet's litter tray? | Leave the tray open to dry | Shake the litter in the air | *Wash your hands | Eat a snack straight away
test: Which word is best for poo in a science report? | Gunk | *Excrement | Stuff | Mess
exam: Which sentence is safe and correct? | Please touch the excrement with bare hands to check it. | Excrement tastes like sweets, so try a little. | Scientists keep excrement in their pockets for fun. | *Please wash your hands well after you clean the litter tray.
